From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: drop debugfs on unregister, not only on destroy

Every audio DSP restart leaves a debugfs collision behind:

    # echo stop > /sys/class/remoteproc/remoteproc0/state
    # echo start > /sys/class/remoteproc/remoteproc0/state
    debugfs: 'pmic_glink.ucsi.0' already exists in 'ucsi'

ucsi_debugfs_register() is called from ucsi_register(), but
ucsi_debugfs_unregister() only from ucsi_destroy(). That pairing holds for an
interface registered once and destroyed once. ucsi_glink is not one: its
interface lives in a protection domain on the ADSP, and
pmic_glink_ucsi_register() calls ucsi_unregister() and ucsi_register() again
on every PDR down/up -- so the second registration finds the directory the
first one left in place.

It is a leak, not just a message. ucsi_debugfs_register() overwrites
ucsi->debugfs with a fresh allocation, so the previous struct and the whole
dentry tree it pointed at become unreachable, once per restart, and the files
left in debugfs are wired to a UCSI instance that is being torn down.

Release it from ucsi_unregister() so the two really pair up, and NULL the
pointer in ucsi_debugfs_unregister() -- without that, ucsi_destroy() following
a ucsi_unregister() would free it a second time.

Placed before the notification-disable so it also acts as a barrier:
debugfs_remove_recursive() waits for a command issued through those files
instead of letting it race the teardown.

Reproducible with a plain SSR; the hibernate path merely performs a
stop/start.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -2366,6 +2366,21 @@
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&ucsi->work);
 	cancel_work_sync(&ucsi->resume_work);
 
+	/*
+	 * Pairs with the ucsi_debugfs_register() in ucsi_register(). Doing it
+	 * from ucsi_destroy() alone is enough for an interface registered
+	 * once, but ucsi_glink unregisters and registers again every time the
+	 * protection domain behind it restarts, and the second registration
+	 * then collides with what the first one left behind --
+	 *
+	 *   debugfs: 'pmic_glink.ucsi.0' already exists in 'ucsi'
+	 *
+	 * -- and overwrites ucsi->debugfs, leaking it and its dentries. Also
+	 * a barrier: debugfs_remove_recursive() waits for a command started
+	 * from there rather than letting it race this teardown.
+	 */
+	ucsi_debugfs_unregister(ucsi);
+
 	/* Disable notifications */
 	ucsi->ops->async_control(ucsi, cmd);
 
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/debugfs.c
@@ -162,6 +162,7 @@
 
 	debugfs_remove_recursive(ucsi->debugfs->dentry);
 	kfree(ucsi->debugfs);
+	ucsi->debugfs = NULL;
 }
 
 void ucsi_debugfs_init(void)
